<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BES hits fresh highs.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BES hits fresh highs.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Espirito Santo continued to gain, propelled forward by good first half results, with the stock hitting a record high of 4,713 escudos on Thursday.</p>
<p>Although it had slipped slightly from the peak to 4,695 escudos at 1252 GMT, it was still 1.62 percent up on the day.</p>
<p>Traders said that investors had been slow to react to the results released early on Tuesday. &quot;But now the buy orders just don't seem to stop,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>The Bank posted a consolidated net profit of 15.2 billion escudos in the first half of 1997, up 43 percent on the same time last year.</p>
<p>--Paula Cordeiro, Lisbon bureau 3511-3113125</p>
